  "status_text": "One circuit can tell whether noisy messages have a decoder and then identify their labels. Lean checked a circuit that takes the allowed clean bits and a received word as inputs for fixed dimensions and per-label loss and gain limits (L-lib-1424). It decides whether the supplied list has a decoder within a fixed NOT cap. Whenever it does, the output identifies the label of each permitted received word. At fixed NOT cap, the gate bound is polynomial in word width and number of labels.",
